# wear/man/apron_hang: the work apron's leather skirt from the belt to mid-thigh, a solid lit hem; it swings a row with
# the step, the front leg pushes it forward in side views, it flaps out in the run, lies on the lap seated
# GARB-M (P2b wave 2); fitted to the man (STYLE_P2 22). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# The side run (leg pass round 2, 2026-10-20): the side flare views (the run) kick the skirt up to the run hem, a row
# under the garment's lifted run views, so the legs show under it as limbs.
# The motion rebuild (2026-10-21, docs/MOTION_P2.md 7): the side walk takes torso=run (the torso's hem a row up), so the
# side `wide` views (contact, down) carry the torso rest's last row on top (no trouser band between torso and skirt) and
# ride the PIVOT (a `when elf` twin a row up): the man's down frames drop his hip a pixel and a hip-anchored hem would
# cover the knees; on the pivot the hem holds its row, as the woman's held hip does. The pass frames' gap row and back
# edge are <garment>_stride.pxm's (keyed by the legs), so the rest views (idle, hurt, falls, postures) are untouched.
use person woman
legend Z linen 4
body man
role garment apron
layer hangFront
anchor hip
keys hang
sway 1

view D key rest origin 5 -2
|fihhhghggf
|fjiiiiihhf
build
|.+.....x+.

